        "severity": "major",
        "evidence": "The Markov normaliser in this block is convention C, in the sqrt-variable spelling the audits are documented to miss. 1/(q^(1/2) + q^(-1/2)) = sqrt(q)/(q+1) = z_C. Verified numerically at the proton pin: 0.4993203341836945 against AGENTS.md quoted z_C(q0) = 0.4993203342, and against z_D(q0) = 0.6126880371. The 2026-08-15 owner ruling makes z_D = q^3/(q^2+1) canonical and excises C. scripts/lean-markov-convention-audit.py does not report this file - the occurrence is inside a class field type rather than a markovZ definition, and uses the sqrt spelling AGENTS.md records as invisible to the shape audits (the qou-t9r1 blindness family).",
        "notes": "Flagged, NOT migrated - deliberately. AGENTS.md is explicit that C-frame results need RE-DERIVATION rather than a z substitution, and that dropping z_D into a C-frame formula is not a valid move (cf. QOU.QBeta.decayLadder_zC_threeRow_ne_zero). The formula is kept exactly as the .md states it and the normaliser is now a named def skeinNormaliserC, labelled convention C at the use site rather than buried in a division, so the next reader sees the frame without re-deriving it. Migration belongs to qou-cds1. Warn rather than fail because the recorded value is correct for the frame it is in; what was missing was the label."
